{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Story B (84c7) implemented via held-out TDD. RED first: 13 tests, 10 failed for the right reasons (criterion/move/prompt/evidence absent); 3 passing were survive-the-change invariants. Held out 12; implementer (standard tier / sonnet, separate subagent) saw only the happy path, reported green on attempt 1, and correctly declined to touch src/rebar. Full oracle then 12/13 with the only failure being the committed-evidence artifact, which is the orchestrator's job (a real review run), NOT an implementer failure - so no tier escalation. ORACLE GAP I then fixed (a test defect, not a model failure): .gitignore ignores .rebar/prompts/* with per-file negations, so the new rubric was UNTRACKED - it worked locally and would have shipped to nobody. Added test_every_overlay_asset_is_tracked_by_git (RED, then the negation line, then GREEN) - this is exactly the silent class the epic exists to catch, and my first oracle missed it. Now 15/16, remaining failure = the evidence doc. Gerrit: 1016 and 1017 both LLM-Review +1, Verified still pending, 0 unresolved comments. Real review-plan run against 061c S1 (7468, --force --no-sign so a closed ticket's attestation is untouched) is in flight to produce the evidence artifact."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785377526412193001,"uuid":"9d54a8ac-7694-425e-aafd-1d52686cc3f7"}